{"complete":true,"school_name":"Mississippi State University","town_name":"Mississippi State","boards":[{"complete":true,"school_name":"Mississippi State University","town_name":"Mississippi State","template_id":"college-first-weekend","title":"Your First Weekend at Mississippi State University, Shared as Cards","description":"A low-pressure, under-21-safe sequence of campus stops that combines orientation, recreation, history, and a few places to revisit once classes begin.","icon":"schedule","cards":[{"subject_id":"msu-drill-field","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"The Drill Field","title":"Start with a campus-orientation lap","subtitle":"Friday afternoon · central campus","notes":"Walk the perimeter, pick out Lee Hall, Swalm Hall, and Mitchell Memorial Library, then use the lawn as your reference point for later meetups.","short_summary":"A central green space that makes the campus layout easier to understand.","evidence_claim":"MSU identifies the historic Drill Field as a popular gathering greenspace at the center of campus.","source_url":"https://www.msstate.edu/about/traditions/drill-field","source_title":"The Drill Field | Mississippi State University","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Outdoor campus greenspace; confirm any event setup or temporary access restrictions on arrival.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"msu-chapel-of-memories","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Chapel of Memories","title":"Pause at the Chapel of Memories","subtitle":"Friday afternoon · near the campus core","notes":"Take a quiet exterior look at the chapel and carillon tower; notice the brickwork, then continue through the nearby central-campus paths.","short_summary":"A historic campus landmark built with brick from Old Main Dormitory.","evidence_claim":"MSU says the chapel was constructed in the mid-